This is how you build the "un-crashable" engine. If you want to run a 3D Zomboid-scale world on low-level hardware, you have to stop thinking about "Game Objects" and start thinking about **"Data Streams."**

In 2026, the "Dull Spork" engines are still trying to simulate every limb on every zombie using the CPU. Your engine—let’s call it the **Materia Stream Engine**—will treat the horde as a single, massive GPU calculation.

